Z||000020||HotFieroGT||12-17-2001||06:53 PM||||Harry_fiero is correct!<P>I had that same knock and did not realize my overflow tank was cracked.  So my car was slowly draining all the coolant out, one day it overheated and blew a head gasket (water in oil) and I had to overhaul the engine.  That is why there is a sticker under the decklid and under the hood about using the proper fill procedure.<P>Brooke<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||JohnF||12-17-2001||07:02 PM||||For $1400?  You're going to get rid of it?  Are you going to replace it?  If so, what $1400 car is going to be any better?  How many $1400 cars are running around out there with a new engine and no interior or exterior damage?<P>If you just need the money, fine.  Just run a local ad and you can get your $1400.  If you intend to replace it, DON'T.  Fix this aggravating problem and be ready for the next.  I guarantee, it will happen!<P>That's life with any 15 year old $1400 car.  <P>New 'vettes don't have these problems.  They just cost more than $1400.||||reg||9
